HOW THIS RUN WAS PRODUCED
-------------------------
  ./tests/functional/b1-target-functional.sh   # arch=target
  ./tests/functional/b2-current-functional.sh  # arch=current
  ./tests/security/b3-target-security.sh       # arch=target
  ./tests/security/b4-current-security.sh      # arch=current
  ./tests/failover/b5-failover.sh              # arch=target AND arch=current

  # architecture switching (see the up.sh note below)
  ./scripts/up.sh current|target && docker compose up -d --build
  ./scripts/wait-ready.sh

  # every client invocation is logged verbatim inside its group section,
  # in the form: $ docker run ... poc-client <args>

  NOTE ON ./scripts/up.sh: it is invoked as `./scripts/up.sh current`,
  but it forwards "$@" to docker compose without shifting the architecture
  argument off first (scripts/up.sh line 51: docker compose up -d --build "$@"),
  so compose fails with 'no such service: current'. up.sh has already written
  ARCH/COMPOSE_PROFILES into .env by then, so the run proceeded with a plain
  'docker compose up -d --build'. Reported, not patched (out of scope).

  RESULTS LAYOUT
  --------------
    tests-run.log            this file
    <group>.txt              full stdout+stderr of one group, PASS/FAIL inline
    <group>-<arch>.stdout    verbatim stdout for runs repeated per architecture
    raw/<group>/*            every raw artifact: client JSON, probe series,
                             VIP ownership series, DNS answers, dig output

    FAILOVER-NOTES.txt       why failover timings come from keepalived's
                             console log and not from the notify hook
